# Admin Ziggy scheme follows APP_URL (marketing only)

**Goal:** Keep admin sidenav / `route()` links on `https://` when the browser is on HTTPS, without breaking tenant subdomain login.

## Why it happens
1. Marketing + admin routes are `Route::domain(...)` scoped.
2. Ziggy then emits **absolute** URLs and takes the scheme/host from `Ziggy.url`.
3. Default Ziggy base URL is `url('/')`, which uses the **incoming request** scheme.
4. TLS often terminates at Apache/nginx, so PHP sees `http` unless `TRUSTED_PROXIES` is set.
5. Result on marketing/admin: page is `https://…` but sidenav hrefs are `http://…`.
6. If Ziggy is always pinned to `APP_URL`, tenant pages (e.g. `boom2.…/login`) post `route('login')` to the marketing host and hit CORS.

## Fix in code
`AdminZiggy::toArray()`:
- **Marketing host:** base URL = `config('app.url')` (https scheme/host).
- **Tenant host:** base URL = request host with scheme from `APP_URL` (keeps subdomain + https).

## Ops (required behind host Apache → :8021)
Set `TRUSTED_PROXIES=*` in `docker/env/app.env` (and host `.env`). Without it Laravel sees a private Docker IP, so Ziggy/https links and IP geo (pricing currency) both fall back wrong. Recreate the app container after changing it.

## Regression
`php artisan test --filter=AdminDashboardShellTest`

## What didn't work
- Treating this as an AdminLayout bug; `route()` was absolute because of domain-scoped routes, not relative paths.
- Pinning every request (including tenants) to `APP_URL`; that fixed admin https but made workspace login POST to the marketing domain.
